From 290330f54ef8addc8a06d882221db9eff3ce835e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: praveen <praveenkumar.shanmugam@amd.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 21:36:29 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] gpu-watch: millisecond power tier and UBB power

Extend the existing GPUWatch create/subscribe API (no new RPC):

- GPUWatchSpec.FastPeriodMs (1, 10, 100 or a multiple of 1000 up to
  60000; 0 = 1000). SlowPeriodSecs is unchanged.
- Per-attribute tiers: the power family (socket power, energy, voltages,
  PPT/thermal residency accumulators, firmware timestamp, system clock
  counter) refreshes every FastPeriodMs; other fast attributes no faster
  than 1 s; ECC/XGMI at SlowPeriodSecs.
- A dedicated smi-power thread reads amdsmi_get_gpu_metrics_info on
  absolute deadlines into a seqlock POWER record. One SMI call in flight
  at a time; below 1000 ms a partial GPUWatch frame (Spec carries only Id)
  is published per GPU right after that GPU is read, through bounded
  per-subscriber queues.
- GPUWatchStatus.MissedTicks counts sampler overruns and ticks dropped
  for a subscriber.
- New attributes: UBB_POWER (140, amdsmi_get_power_info ubb_power,
  partition 0 only, no node handle), FIRMWARE_TIMESTAMP (141),
  SYSTEM_CLOCK_COUNTER (142).
- gpuagent_mock watcher support for the above.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
